    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0418" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/7573: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-04T11:00:00-05:00">July 4, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>550. My telegram No. 546, July 3, 9 a.m.<anchor n="77" xml:id="d432-f1"/> I am
                    confidentially informed that at last night’s Cabinet Council Meeting an
                    agreement is said to have been reached which changes the rubber agreement
                    substantially in favor of Ecuador. As today is a holiday we do not expect
                    details until Monday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
